 "autodetect_pages": "2-37:vn1,39-74:vn2,76-111:vc",
 "notes": "The three 'manuscript' PDFs of UR Research's record, joined vn1, vn2, bass. The trios run in the copy's order (G. 83, 86, 84, 85, 87, 88), not Gerard's: give autopair --quartets in this order. Every movement starts a page, except G. 85's finale (Allegro), which starts on the minuet's page (staff 8) in vn1 and the bass. The bass part is headed 'Basso' and is the cello part (RISM: vlc; Philhar: Violoncelle); it mixes bass and tenor clef. Left out: the record's '(print)' files (the bound-with Venice print of G. 89-94) and colour covers. Some pages begin with empty ruled staves: staff numbers count staves with music."
}
